      "title": "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ab5e4244-481d-50f6-b24c-4473c36c5c07",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $y=1$ is the minimum value of the function.\n- **II.** $x=3\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote of the function.\n- **III.** The function takes the value $-1$ at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a5307c9d-a232-5580-b215-f01d7ed2ba26",
          ":answer-field/key": "I",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "e791140d-ed42-57ee-a199-a98cf2c92f33",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "8fe9807c-6d11-58e2-9caa-a9b52d1fe80b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "e791140d-ed42-57ee-a199-a98cf2c92f33"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "e16e1e61-18c9-5685-964d-5d5bd5d9bf34",
          ":answer-field/key": "II",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "e7264bc6-3b02-5ad2-8151-9f2a567c5fa8",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "002c2714-6d43-5c44-a96f-8160e688c0d2",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "002c2714-6d43-5c44-a96f-8160e688c0d2"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "d6a8c18f-3996-5926-830c-0bf9707d6b23",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "48b21ccc-9f7a-5ef2-b23a-140bc4924624",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "31a54ba2-13b9-5878-8fd6-b5403499b525",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "31a54ba2-13b9-5878-8fd6-b5403499b525"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "d2edddc2-009c-5aa4-9771-202927932263",
          ":answer-field/key": "None of the above",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "9d63889c-efe5-5754-a69f-96df7da2dd15",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "6107b660-a5ca-52ee-8dcd-4cdd667a4bef",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "9d63889c-efe5-5754-a69f-96df7da2dd15"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/06/066fe6ce8a65927436d64753ec4e61bfea257405e4b2f81554ac8341572bcf15.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty )$, therefore the function doesn't have a minimum value. Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi $ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence statement II is true.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $-1$ at $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi .$ Hence statement III is true.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
    },
    "generation": {
