            "f5b2623b-cb4e-5c21-9f4d-908cdb87dee8"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "d65c3f43-d786-524f-9dc2-d03340b50281",
          ":answer-field/key": "III",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "ee2c99d4-da46-5efe-943a-068cfd7154fc",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "d1a1b85a-2652-5973-b8c7-f4938e9e2ca8",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "ee2c99d4-da46-5efe-943a-068cfd7154fc"
          ]
        },
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "52d023ec-bd8c-5f04-a70c-4b7fdba4dea2",
          ":answer-field/key": "None of the above",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/checkbox",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "0668eba2-86c7-5c1c-80aa-cdb8eb6eba7b",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "false"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "66b01d0a-3cef-5db5-9946-f2f3f23f0d16",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/text",
              ":answer/value": "true"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "0668eba2-86c7-5c1c-80aa-cdb8eb6eba7b"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [1,\\infty ).$ Hence, statement I is false.\n\n- The period of the function is $2\\pi ,$ so $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x+2n\\pi )$ for any integer $n.$ Substituing $n=-5,$ we get $\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{csc}⁡(x-10\\pi ).$ Hence, Statement II is true.\n\n- The function $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x$ is defined for all real numbers except the integer multiples of $\\pi ,$ so $-15\\pi $ is not in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.$ Hence, statement III is false.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate"
    },
